7. APPLY REJECTS STALE/CANCELLED/REPLAYED/TAMPERED — REFUTED, holds up.
   `TestSpendingApplyRejections` (spending_optimizer_test.go) covers exactly this matrix — expired,
   cancelled, revision (stale), fingerprint, scenario-switch, manager-swap, unknown/forged token,
   baseline, disqualified (`failed`), missing-policy — 10 subtests, all asserting 409 + no bytes
   written; ran it: PASS (`go test ... -run TestSpendingApplyRejections -v` → all 10 subtests PASS).
   Traced handleApplySpendingOptimizerWithHook: the POST body is read only for `request_id` and
   `recommendation` (a lookup key into a per-preview, server-generated opaque token map) — no financial
   field is ever read from the client for Apply; the actual `MonthlyLivingExpenses`/`LivingSpendingBoost`/
   `Guardrails` written to disk come from the frozen server-held candidate `c`, so tampered posted
   numbers have no effect. On success the preview entry is deleted before the response is sent
   (discardSpendingPreview under the same operation lock, before the deferred applying-flag reset, before
   the deferred unlock), so a replay of the identical POST finds `p == nil` and is rejected — verified
   this is single-use, not just single-concurrent-use.

8. CURRENT-MONTH (`use_current_month`) INTERACTION WITH A SAVED BOOST STOP MONTH — REFUTED, holds up.
   Found and ran `TestSpendingIntegrationPreviewGraphApplyReload` (spending_integration_test.go), which
   ends by manually advancing a saved plan's StartDate past its own saved boost's StopMonth ("2027-10"
   vs. stop "2027-09") via an ordinary `rm.Save`, then asserts the reloaded settings' `LivingSpendingBoost
   .StopMonth` is UNCHANGED ("2027-09", not silently moved) and that `engine.LivingExpensesAtMonth` at
   month 0 has dropped by ~$1000 (the boost's own contribution), confirming the boost goes inert without
   its own schedule being mutated. Ran it standalone: PASS, 13.7s, reproducing the exact seeds named in
   the checker-tests brief (search=20260910, selection=-6884282663016313855, final=-1800455987195215627,
   cut/floor/unpaid=0/0/0) — this is also the test whose fixture the manifest's "one-line fixture fix"
   (`s.UseCurrentMonth = false`) targets; the commit that landed it mid-session (aad72de, "pin the
   spending fixture's start date under use_current_month") explicitly states the untouched fixture let
   the newly-defaulted `use_current_month=true` silently reset the test's own pinned StartDate and
   "reactivated the boost" — i.e. the worker found and fixed exactly this interaction, and the guard test
   for it passes.

